      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll start by reading the original test and the CUT source to understand the code.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. All test data rows crammed onto a single line\n2. Unused data providers and helper methods (`data_badParse`, `data_withNanoOfDay`, `data_plus`, `data_minus`, `doTest_comparisons_UtcInstant`)\n3. No row-level context to explain what each scenario exercises\n\nI'll write a clean version with formatted data rows, remove dead code, and add a `@DisplayName`.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused data providers and helper methods, formats each test-data row on its own line with alignment, renames the anonymous `i` variable to `base` for clarity, adds a `@DisplayName` annotation, and includes a Javadoc comment explaining each column — all while preserving the exact same method calls and assertions."
